pdoom-video
-----------
https://github.com/mexicat/pdoom-video
Copyright (c) 2026 Giacomo Magnanini. MIT License.

The video engine, preview player and render pipeline in
skills/code-video/assets/template-webgl/ (src/engine/, src/main.ts,
scripts/render.ts and the files around them) are adapted from pdoom-video's
app/ folder: from upstream commit bdbad53 and a later copy that added the
render verify mode, accented stroke-font letters, scene remixes, longer
timelines and spliced soundtracks. Each project made with audara-studio keeps
the engine's MIT notice in src/engine/LICENSE.

The engine guide, the treatment and style templates and the GLSL cookbook in
skills/code-video/references/ adapt pdoom-video's docs/ENGINE.md and
docs/TREATMENT.md and link to its scenes. The soundtrack scripts build on the
approach of its analysis/ tools.

motion-video-kit
----------------
https://github.com/echris6/motion-video-kit
Copyright (c) 2026 echris6. MIT License.

Its text and algorithms are adapted in:
- skills/code-video/references/critique.md: the critic protocol and its
  prompts;
- skills/code-video/references/motion.md: the motion craft;
- skills/code-video/scripts/qc.py: the measured checks;
- skills/soundtrack/references/elevenlabs.md: the music and sound-effect
  rules;
- skills/soundtrack/scripts/mix.py: the per-effect level solver and the mix
  rules.

